course: dictionary
lesson: 10762
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word used is a good example. «Isaac Newton's laws of motion are still used to send rockets into space.» Here used means put to work for a purpose. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence instead? Try "put to work" and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Used is also the past form of use. «She used her pen to write the story» tells you that she already did the using. Look at the words before and after used. If they are about doing something, it is probably the verb use.
explain: Used can also describe something that is not new, like «a used car» or a used book. Someone owned it before you. «Alice was getting so used to queer things happening» is a different meaning again: she was no longer surprised by them, because she had met them so often. The little word to after used is a clue too.
fact: Used is the past form of use: «she used her pen».
fact: Used can mean not new, owned before by someone else: «a used car».
fact: «Used to» plus a verb tells about something that happened often in the past but not now: «I used to live in Ohio».
fact: «Be used to» means know something well, so it is not strange: «I am used to the cold».
fact: To check your meaning, swap in a word such as "employed", "second-hand", "in the past" or "familiar" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Stork nests are used year after year and grow huge.» What does used mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Put to use again and again, the same nest every year | Thrown away after one year | Empty and never visited
exercise: «Alice was getting so used to queer things happening.» What does used to mean here? | *Not surprised by them any more | Very tired of them | Good at using them | Afraid of them
exercise: Ben used 6 of his 20 pencils. What does used mean here? | Given back to the shop | *Taken and put to use, so they are no longer in the pot | Borrowed from a friend | Lost forever in a drawer
test: «Mia bought a used bike for her birthday.» What does used tell you about the bike? | Brand new from the factory | It goes faster than other bikes | It is painted red | *It was owned by someone else before
test: «I used to live in Ohio.» What does used to tell us? | Something that is happening right now | Something that will happen next year | Something that never happened | *Something that happened often in the past, but not now
exam: «I am used to the cold.» What does be used to mean? | Hate the cold | *Know the cold well, so it does not feel strange | Like the cold very much | Feel cold all the time
